    "question": {
      ":question/id": "c89bd65a-1c22-5c20-9a49-d8b0dc375adf",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate the line integral of $f(x,y)=3 y$ along the curve\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 2 t^{2},t\\rangle,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le \\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nGive the exact value.\n\nUse the scalar line integral formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm ds &=\\int_a^b f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\text{d}s &=\\int_a^b f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\,\\|\\mathbf{r}'(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{r}(t)=(2 t^{2})\\,\\mathbf{i}+(t)\\,\\mathbf{j}$, then along the curve we have $x=2 t^{2}$, $y=t$.\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf{r}'(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{r}'(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t^{2})\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =(4 t)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(1)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ \\|\\mathbf{r}'(t)\\| & =\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(4 t)^2+(1)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16 t^{2} + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=3 y$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =(3)(t) \\\\  & =3 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int_C f\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\,\\|\\mathbf{r}'(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}(3 t)(\\sqrt{16 t^{2} + 1})\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=16 t^{2} + 1$, $\\text{d}u=(32 t)\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={\\int }_{1}^{33}\\frac{3}{32}\\cdot u^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{32}\\cdot\\frac{2}{3}u^{3/2}\\big|_{1}^{33} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}[(33)^{3/2}-(1)^{3/2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}[(33 \\sqrt{33})-(1)] \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{33 \\sqrt{33}}{16}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{1}{16}\\right) \\\\  & =- \\frac{1}{16} + \\frac{33 \\sqrt{33}}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
